  "topic": "Read and write Ain (ع) at the beginning, middle and end of words, with Fatha, Kasra and Damma.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "learn": [
    {
      "en": "This is Ain. A deep throat sound, like saying 'ah' while tightening your throat. No English equivalent!",
      "title": "Meet Ain!",
      "ar": "ع",
      "aud": "c-0-ar",
      "tr": "Ain"
    },
    {
      "en": "Looks like a small eye or fishhook: an open curve at the top that closes at the bottom. Ain means EYE in Arabic and the letter looks like an eye! Say it from your throat.",
      "title": "How to write Ain"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a fatha, Ain says “a”.",
      "title": "Ain with fatha",
      "ar": "عَ",
      "aud": "c-2-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a kasra, Ain says “e”.",
      "title": "Ain with kasra",
      "ar": "عِ",
      "aud": "c-3-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a damma, Ain says “o”.",
      "title": "Ain with damma",
      "ar": "عُ",
      "aud": "c-4-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "“Knowledge is light”",
      "title": "Sentence of the lesson",
      "ar": "العِلْمُ نُورٌ",
      "aud": "c-5-ar",
      "tr": "Al-ʿelme Noor"
    }
  ],
